# CSS & Tailwind Standards

- **`src/styles/starwind.css`**: Starwind theme tokens only (brand `--primary` overrides OK).
- **`src/styles/global.css`**: App entry — imports Starwind, fluid tokens, fonts, nav/FAQ project styles.
- Do not overwrite `--fluid-min-width` or `--fluid-max-width` unless specifically requested.
- Maintain existing `--fluid-bp` calculations for responsive scaling.
- Layout imports **only** `global.css`.

## Bare / canonical values over brackets (Tailwind v4)

Prefer bare custom values (and spacing-scale forms) whenever Tailwind can express them without brackets. Unnecessary `[…]` triggers `suggestCanonicalClasses` warnings.

Use brackets **only** for complex CSS syntax (multi-part values, `calc()`, `url()`, etc.). Prefer fluid tokens from `global.css` over raw px when spacing is involved.

```html
<!-- ❌ BAD — unnecessary brackets (warns) -->
<div class="flex-[29] top-[117px]">…</div>

<!-- ✅ GOOD — bare / canonical -->
<div class="flex-29 top-29.25">…</div>

<!-- ✅ OK — brackets needed (complex CSS) -->
<div class="grid-cols-[1fr_500px_2fr] w-[calc(100%-2rem)] bg-[url('/hero.png')]">…</div>

<!-- ✅ OK — CSS variable shorthand -->
<div class="bg-(--my-brand)">…</div>
```

Ref: [Adding custom styles](https://tailwindcss.com/docs/adding-custom-styles) — bare values vs arbitrary `[…]` values.

## Color tokens

Prefer semantic classes mapped in `starwind.css` (`@theme inline` → `--color-*`) instead of raw palette colors with manual dark variants.

```html
<!-- ❌ BAD — hardcoded zinc + dark: -->
<p class="text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300">…</p>

<!-- ✅ GOOD — token handles light/dark -->
<p class="text-muted-foreground">…</p>

<!-- ❌ BAD — paired token outside its context -->
<div class="bg-primary-foreground">…</div>

<!-- ✅ GOOD — literal white/black -->
<div class="bg-white">…</div>
```

Useful tokens: `background`, `foreground`, `muted`, `muted-foreground`, `card`, `border`, `primary`, `secondary`, `accent`, `destructive`/`error`, etc.

**Exception:** for straight white/black (not a themed surface), use `bg-white` / `bg-black` (or `text-white` / `text-black`). Do not use `*-primary-foreground` (or similar paired tokens) when you are not on a primary-colored element.
